1
00:00:01,520 --> 00:00:03,920
THIS SHOW IS CREATED
FOR ENTERTAINMENT PURPOSES ONLY

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,360
THE CHARACTERS, BEHAVIORS
AND EVENTS ARE FICTITIOUS

3
00:00:06,440 --> 00:00:08,560
THEY ARE NOT INTENDED TO
DEFAME OR CAUSE DAMAGE

4
00:00:08,640 --> 00:00:10,920
TO ANY ORGANIZATION OR INDIVIDUAL.
VIEWER DISCRETION IS ADVISED.

5
00:02:25,400 --> 00:02:27,880
Are you trying to shake up
the whole bureau?

6
00:02:28,680 --> 00:02:29,960
<i>If we give him time,</i>

7
00:02:30,040 --> 00:02:31,280
<i>he'll get off the hook again.</i>

8
00:02:33,120 --> 00:02:35,440
Isn't that Paisan with Robert,
the gambling site owner?

9
00:02:35,520 --> 00:02:36,960
Care to clarify this now?

10
00:02:37,560 --> 00:02:40,080
Please come with us
to address what happened.

11
00:02:41,040 --> 00:02:44,240
Are you… going to kill him?

12
00:02:47,480 --> 00:02:48,960
You broke in here. What do you want?

13
00:02:49,560 --> 00:02:51,960
I'll give you a chance

14
00:02:52,560 --> 00:02:53,880
<i>to survive.</i>

15
00:02:59,840 --> 00:03:01,000
I work for Robert.

16
00:03:03,920 --> 00:03:08,400
But he's actually just a small fry.

17
00:03:11,440 --> 00:03:14,720
The real big boss behind everything

18
00:03:15,320 --> 00:03:17,800
is Seehan and…

19
00:03:39,480 --> 00:03:40,720
Huh? Hey!

20
00:03:55,440 --> 00:03:56,600
Stop right there, sir.

21
00:03:57,520 --> 00:03:58,760
Surrender.

22
00:06:21,040 --> 00:06:22,200
Gun. Hey.

23
00:06:23,080 --> 00:06:23,960
Gun.

24
00:06:24,840 --> 00:06:25,760
Hey, stop!

25
00:06:29,280 --> 00:06:30,240
Gun.

26
00:06:31,480 --> 00:06:32,400
Gun.

27
00:06:40,520 --> 00:06:41,640
Hey!

28
00:06:42,280 --> 00:06:44,600
Gun. Stop, Gun!

29
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:00,040
Hey, watch out!

30
00:07:00,120 --> 00:07:01,200
Whoa.

31
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:06,040
Gun.

32
00:07:44,880 --> 00:07:46,800
Seehan really leaves no loose ends.

33
00:07:47,440 --> 00:07:49,320
Anyone who's useless gets wiped out.

34
00:07:52,040 --> 00:07:53,720
The team sent to kill Paisan

35
00:07:55,360 --> 00:07:56,640
wasn't Seehan's.

36
00:07:59,640 --> 00:08:00,600
Whose team then?

37
00:08:02,600 --> 00:08:04,120
Someone powerful enough

38
00:08:05,080 --> 00:08:06,600
to take out both cops

39
00:08:07,960 --> 00:08:09,320
and people like us.

40
00:08:21,200 --> 00:08:24,240
I'm sorry we had to lose Paisan

41
00:08:26,040 --> 00:08:28,000
and that we're down another man.

42
00:08:35,880 --> 00:08:37,760
Are you really sorry

43
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:41,679
or disappointed your guy
failed to silence him?

44
00:08:45,120 --> 00:08:47,760
Actually, I think
it's good for our operation.

45
00:08:48,520 --> 00:08:50,720
We need people we can trust.

46
00:08:54,280 --> 00:08:55,120
You're right.

47
00:08:57,400 --> 00:08:58,840
This is good for us.

48
00:09:00,840 --> 00:09:02,200
One less cut to make.

49
00:09:06,360 --> 00:09:08,800
But I want Paisan's share.

50
00:09:17,840 --> 00:09:19,520
I have no problem with that at all.

51
00:09:20,840 --> 00:09:22,520
We're working together,

52
00:09:23,280 --> 00:09:25,480
so we expect a bigger return.

53
00:09:26,920 --> 00:09:29,440
You want a bigger piece of the pie?

54
00:09:30,640 --> 00:09:32,800
Submit a proposal
to open the border for me.

55
00:09:36,920 --> 00:09:39,160
That's already part of my plan.

56
00:10:04,880 --> 00:10:06,440
FOR THE PUBLIC

57
00:10:06,520 --> 00:10:07,840
Oh, sir.

58
00:10:07,920 --> 00:10:09,440
What did the higher-ups say?

59
00:10:10,520 --> 00:10:11,760
I got chewed out.

60
00:10:13,720 --> 00:10:15,040
The suspect died in front of me.

61
00:10:16,760 --> 00:10:17,920
Was it Seehan?

62
00:10:21,320 --> 00:10:23,040
Those shots weren't fired by amateurs.

63
00:10:23,880 --> 00:10:25,280
They're definitely trained.

64
00:10:26,680 --> 00:10:27,880
Are they law enforcement?

65
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:31,880
Right now, we need to arrest Gun first.

66
00:10:33,200 --> 00:10:34,760
But Gun has never shot at us.

67
00:10:35,480 --> 00:10:39,040
When we helped them that time,
he only fired his gun to escape.

68
00:10:39,680 --> 00:10:41,680
And that night, he saved your life.

69
00:10:43,120 --> 00:10:45,040
I think instead of focusing on Gun,

70
00:10:45,120 --> 00:10:47,640
we should focus on Seehan
and law enforcement.

71
00:10:48,320 --> 00:10:51,160
Yeah, I know how to separate the two.

72
00:10:52,040 --> 00:10:53,840
But right now, Gun's the only one

73
00:10:53,920 --> 00:10:56,520
who might know
who's pulling all the strings.

74
00:10:57,440 --> 00:10:58,840
We need to find him right away.

75
00:11:00,400 --> 00:11:02,040
So, where should we begin?

76
00:11:07,560 --> 00:11:08,560
Hey.

77
00:11:09,640 --> 00:11:11,720
I forgot about someone close to Gun.

78
00:12:34,720 --> 00:12:37,000
Okay, I'll be right there.

79
00:12:37,600 --> 00:12:38,840
Where are you going?

80
00:12:40,960 --> 00:12:44,440
I'm not trying to pry into your business.

81
00:12:44,520 --> 00:12:46,040
I'm just worried.

82
00:12:48,920 --> 00:12:52,400
If there's anything
I can help with, tell me.

83
00:12:52,480 --> 00:12:54,240
I want to help you too.

84
00:13:23,200 --> 00:13:24,280
I'm almost there.

85
00:13:48,520 --> 00:13:49,880
I'm here.

86
00:15:03,480 --> 00:15:06,480
What would you like to eat, sir?
Why not just order through the app?

87
00:15:08,480 --> 00:15:10,640
No need to waste time
coming all the way here.

88
00:15:14,400 --> 00:15:15,480
Where is Gun?

89
00:15:17,640 --> 00:15:19,080
If he wanted to see you,

90
00:15:19,160 --> 00:15:22,640
you wouldn't need to follow me like this.

91
00:16:06,600 --> 00:16:08,440
My ride's fast. You'll never catch me.

92
00:16:21,400 --> 00:16:22,640
I'm here.

93
00:16:23,440 --> 00:16:24,960
Someone followed me.

94
00:16:26,520 --> 00:16:27,800
Who?

95
00:16:27,880 --> 00:16:29,480
Probably Sarawut.

96
00:16:29,560 --> 00:16:30,880
Don't come to the spot yet.

97
00:16:31,680 --> 00:16:32,640
Yeah.

98
00:16:33,560 --> 00:16:34,640
I know the drill.

99
00:16:42,360 --> 00:16:44,160
I asked, where is Gun?

100
00:16:45,960 --> 00:16:46,800
Listen.

101
00:16:48,160 --> 00:16:52,240
I'm not married to the guy.
How would I know?

102
00:16:52,840 --> 00:16:53,960
Do you know

103
00:16:54,880 --> 00:16:56,840
Gun is breaking the law?

104
00:16:58,360 --> 00:17:00,000
We're civil servants.

105
00:17:01,400 --> 00:17:04,119
No one wants to break the law
unless backed into a corner.

106
00:17:05,040 --> 00:17:09,440
Saying this means
you're siding with Gun.

107
00:17:12,280 --> 00:17:14,160
That makes you an accomplice.

108
00:17:17,680 --> 00:17:18,800
Easy there, kid.

109
00:17:19,839 --> 00:17:22,000
Don't use the law
against someone you know.

110
00:17:25,560 --> 00:17:29,200
I could use the law
to call you in for questioning.

111
00:17:29,280 --> 00:17:33,240
But I won't do that
because we know each other.

112
00:17:34,080 --> 00:17:36,440
I want Gun to turn himself in,

113
00:17:38,120 --> 00:17:40,760
tell the truth, and fight this legally.

114
00:17:42,640 --> 00:17:43,920
The law is great,

115
00:17:45,640 --> 00:17:47,440
as long as the people
enforcing it are good.

116
00:17:50,080 --> 00:17:51,440
But if one day

117
00:17:54,040 --> 00:17:56,920
the people using it aren't good

118
00:17:58,400 --> 00:18:00,880
and use it for selfish gain
or to help their cronies…

119
00:18:00,960 --> 00:18:02,200
That's not me.

120
00:18:03,960 --> 00:18:05,280
I use it to protect the good.

121
00:18:05,360 --> 00:18:06,760
Then you have to protect Gun.

122
00:18:08,440 --> 00:18:11,000
He's destroying those
who hide behind the law

123
00:18:11,080 --> 00:18:12,800
and a system that's about to collapse.

124
00:18:13,400 --> 00:18:15,640
Instead of wasting time hunting him down,

125
00:18:15,720 --> 00:18:18,000
why not find evidence
against the bad guys?

126
00:18:18,080 --> 00:18:20,040
Yeah, I'll definitely do my best on that.

127
00:18:22,600 --> 00:18:25,600
But if you don't help
and keep getting in my way,

128
00:18:26,320 --> 00:18:27,400
you're guilty too.

129
00:18:27,480 --> 00:18:29,080
Are you threatening me?

130
00:18:29,800 --> 00:18:31,120
I'm not.

131
00:18:32,400 --> 00:18:33,800
I'm just doing my duty.

132
00:18:33,880 --> 00:18:36,720
Protecting a friend is my duty too.

133
00:18:38,160 --> 00:18:39,320
I warned you.

134
00:18:47,880 --> 00:18:51,960
If you have evidence,
arrest me.

135
00:18:53,880 --> 00:18:54,800
Do it.

136
00:18:55,800 --> 00:18:57,760
Do it! Do it!

137
00:18:57,840 --> 00:18:59,360
Yeah!

138
00:18:59,440 --> 00:19:02,720
I will. But not now.

139
00:19:09,160 --> 00:19:10,120
I'll be waiting.

140
00:19:34,040 --> 00:19:35,600
I'm going out.

141
00:19:36,200 --> 00:19:38,200
Want anything to eat? I'll buy it for you.

142
00:19:43,120 --> 00:19:44,480
Anything is fine.

143
00:19:46,800 --> 00:19:50,120
That is actually the hardest option.

144
00:19:52,760 --> 00:19:53,840
Sorry.

145
00:19:55,400 --> 00:19:58,640
I'll have sukiyaki soup then.

146
00:20:01,080 --> 00:20:02,320
Uh, hey…

147
00:20:04,840 --> 00:20:05,840
What is it?

148
00:20:06,760 --> 00:20:11,240
Can I ask for one more thing?

149
00:20:14,000 --> 00:20:15,640
Go left. Great.

150
00:20:16,280 --> 00:20:18,720
Not there, man. Damn it.

151
00:20:22,360 --> 00:20:24,560
Follow me. Go left.

152
00:20:26,040 --> 00:20:26,880
Go, go, go.

153
00:20:35,920 --> 00:20:38,960
If you try to run, I'll shoot you.

154
00:20:50,040 --> 00:20:51,520
And I won't help you.

155
00:20:56,680 --> 00:20:58,400
-Ouch.
-Here.

156
00:20:58,480 --> 00:20:59,880
Sit still.

157
00:21:02,120 --> 00:21:05,800
Thanks a lot. Your bullets are awesome.

158
00:21:06,680 --> 00:21:08,400
They have a longer range
than the ones I had.

159
00:21:09,000 --> 00:21:10,080
They work?

160
00:21:13,840 --> 00:21:16,520
That's taken. Shipping it out tonight.

161
00:21:21,560 --> 00:21:22,800
That one too.

162
00:21:27,360 --> 00:21:28,720
And the armor-piercing rounds?

163
00:21:29,600 --> 00:21:30,600
Out of stock.

164
00:21:36,800 --> 00:21:37,760
Hey.

165
00:21:38,960 --> 00:21:42,000
Does your stuff sell that well? Huh?

166
00:21:48,200 --> 00:21:51,640
Just a marketing tactic, man.
It actually doesn't sell at all.

167
00:22:16,560 --> 00:22:18,920
Sir, still no leads on Gun.

168
00:22:21,000 --> 00:22:25,360
The law is great
if the people using it are still good.

169
00:22:26,640 --> 00:22:28,040
But if one day

170
00:22:29,480 --> 00:22:32,240
the people using it aren't good…

171
00:22:33,280 --> 00:22:34,120
Sir.

172
00:22:35,600 --> 00:22:37,120
-Sir.
-Yeah, yeah.

173
00:22:37,200 --> 00:22:38,280
Hey.

174
00:22:38,800 --> 00:22:40,560
Keep track of General Decha's movements.

175
00:22:40,640 --> 00:22:41,520
Got it.

176
00:22:42,280 --> 00:22:43,280
Get everything.

177
00:22:44,640 --> 00:22:47,480
Finances, people he meets,
routes he takes.

178
00:22:47,560 --> 00:22:48,520
Yes, sir.

179
00:23:37,160 --> 00:23:38,720
I'll go get the plates.

180
00:23:54,240 --> 00:23:55,760
You really bought it.

181
00:23:59,240 --> 00:24:00,400
Thank you.

182
00:24:08,520 --> 00:24:09,840
That's not enough?

183
00:25:35,280 --> 00:25:37,160
Why do you want a cactus?

184
00:25:43,120 --> 00:25:46,200
It's a lot like me.

185
00:25:47,520 --> 00:25:50,080
It doesn't need much care to grow.

186
00:25:50,760 --> 00:25:53,240
All it needs is a little light.

187
00:25:55,480 --> 00:25:58,240
But when it blooms, it's beautiful.

188
00:26:00,800 --> 00:26:03,040
What about you? Do you like it?

189
00:26:08,120 --> 00:26:09,120
I like it.

190
00:26:10,720 --> 00:26:13,360
Do you like the cactus or do you like me?

191
00:26:17,320 --> 00:26:18,280
The cactus.

192
00:26:20,600 --> 00:26:24,080
Really? You don't like me?

193
00:26:29,640 --> 00:26:30,880
I like the cactus.

194
00:26:32,080 --> 00:26:33,720
Are you sure you don't like me?

195
00:26:35,680 --> 00:26:36,800
Do you like me?

196
00:26:38,440 --> 00:26:39,360
Do you like me or not?

197
00:26:40,120 --> 00:26:41,160
What about now?

198
00:26:48,360 --> 00:26:49,640
You ask a lot of questions.

199
00:27:12,920 --> 00:27:16,840
Seehan's group has a meeting
at the youth training center.

200
00:27:18,240 --> 00:27:19,400
Why are they going there?

201
00:27:20,440 --> 00:27:23,280
The Dreams for the Future
Foundation event.

202
00:27:24,840 --> 00:27:26,440
Decha is presiding over the opening.

203
00:27:27,160 --> 00:27:28,960
After the ceremony,

204
00:27:29,040 --> 00:27:31,920
they will sign the papers
to launch the border project.

205
00:27:33,440 --> 00:27:36,800
If it gets signed, we're all screwed.
There's no way to block scammers.

206
00:27:38,400 --> 00:27:42,080
Paisan just died.
They must be on high alert.

207
00:29:09,760 --> 00:29:11,200
See anything unusual?

208
00:29:11,800 --> 00:29:12,800
Nothing yet, sir.

209
00:29:14,720 --> 00:29:15,800
And you?

210
00:29:24,680 --> 00:29:25,720
Still clear.

211
00:29:26,760 --> 00:29:30,120
Secure all positions. Anything
goes wrong, you're held responsible.

212
00:29:30,720 --> 00:29:31,920
Understood.

213
00:29:32,000 --> 00:29:33,120
Understood.

214
00:29:38,000 --> 00:29:40,120
The boss called you in
for an important mission.

215
00:29:40,200 --> 00:29:44,000
He believes Gun will show up here.
If you see him, take him out.

216
00:29:47,440 --> 00:29:48,640
Give me your phone.

217
00:29:49,400 --> 00:29:51,200
No personal communication
devices on this mission.

218
00:30:20,800 --> 00:30:23,480
Hello. Ah, hello, kids.

219
00:30:39,120 --> 00:30:40,160
Target spotted.

220
00:30:46,280 --> 00:30:47,360
Ladies and gentlemen.

221
00:30:47,440 --> 00:30:49,240
TWENTY-FIFTH ANNIVERSARY
REINTEGRATING GOOD CITIZENS

222
00:30:49,320 --> 00:30:51,880
First of all, I'd like to thank everyone

223
00:30:51,960 --> 00:30:54,040
for taking the time to be here today.

224
00:30:54,120 --> 00:30:56,600
Whenever I have the chance to come here,

225
00:30:57,880 --> 00:31:01,680
I don't see kids who made mistakes.

226
00:31:02,880 --> 00:31:04,400
Instead, I see

227
00:31:05,200 --> 00:31:06,960
kids who need an opportunity.

228
00:31:09,840 --> 00:31:12,040
All units, take him out.

229
00:31:20,320 --> 00:31:21,280
Target missed.

230
00:31:22,720 --> 00:31:24,480
Methee, shoot him.

231
00:31:42,720 --> 00:31:43,720
Target missed.

232
00:31:47,840 --> 00:31:49,120
Don't let him escape.

233
00:31:54,400 --> 00:31:58,240
Thank you to all involved for working
together to make this project a success.

234
00:31:58,320 --> 00:32:00,240
Especially the private sector

235
00:32:01,360 --> 00:32:03,440
for jointly building this training center

236
00:32:03,520 --> 00:32:06,880
to give our youth a good future.

237
00:32:06,960 --> 00:32:09,440
TWENTY-FIFTH ANNIVERSARY
REINTEGRATING GOOD CITIZENS

238
00:32:13,280 --> 00:32:15,480
Sir, the meeting room is ready.

239
00:32:22,440 --> 00:32:24,240
Hey, he's here. Follow him!

240
00:32:28,240 --> 00:32:29,440
Search everywhere.

241
00:32:37,040 --> 00:32:39,440
Hey! You!

242
00:32:59,320 --> 00:33:00,640
Report the situation.

243
00:33:02,520 --> 00:33:05,160
Why are you quiet? Report in!

244
00:33:05,240 --> 00:33:06,680
Too bad.

245
00:33:23,280 --> 00:33:24,520
Methee!

246
00:33:28,920 --> 00:33:30,280
You missed on purpose, huh?

247
00:33:32,360 --> 00:33:34,880
Come on, everyone makes mistakes.

248
00:33:34,960 --> 00:33:36,120
Mistake my ass.

249
00:33:37,840 --> 00:33:40,360
Yes, he's my best friend.
I don't let that cloud my judgment.

250
00:33:40,440 --> 00:33:43,120
Judgment, my ass. What's this?

251
00:33:43,920 --> 00:33:45,280
You've been in contact with him.

252
00:33:49,400 --> 00:33:52,680
Take him away.
Let General Decha deal with him later.

253
00:34:06,920 --> 00:34:07,960
Finish him.

254
00:34:36,239 --> 00:34:37,600
What's up?

255
00:34:38,239 --> 00:34:40,239
Bro, I need to talk to the boss.

256
00:34:41,120 --> 00:34:43,000
Just say it. I'll tell him myself.

257
00:34:43,560 --> 00:34:46,239
It's very important.
I need to talk to him.

258
00:34:51,000 --> 00:34:54,360
Sir, Pasin has something
important to tell you.

259
00:34:55,679 --> 00:34:56,880
Hello.

260
00:34:57,920 --> 00:34:59,080
Hello.

261
00:34:59,160 --> 00:35:01,480
-Hello.
-We got here almost at the same time.

262
00:35:01,560 --> 00:35:03,880
The boss is busy.
Whatever it is, just tell me.

263
00:35:04,480 --> 00:35:05,920
Tell the boss that Methee is--

264
00:35:21,600 --> 00:35:22,640
Tell the boss what?

265
00:35:24,640 --> 00:35:27,440
Pasin wants me to tell you
that everything is fine here.

266
00:35:27,960 --> 00:35:30,080
Then why didn't he say it himself?

267
00:35:33,080 --> 00:35:36,240
He's taking a dump, sir.

268
00:35:59,760 --> 00:36:02,080
Let's not waste time.
Let's go inside to talk

269
00:36:02,160 --> 00:36:04,040
and sign the documents right away.

270
00:36:04,120 --> 00:36:05,320
-Good idea.
-How about that?

271
00:36:05,400 --> 00:36:06,560
-Sure.
-Let's go.

272
00:36:06,640 --> 00:36:07,480
Please.

273
00:36:10,120 --> 00:36:10,960
‎Ah.

274
00:36:14,560 --> 00:36:16,920
I received orders
to provide security here.

275
00:36:18,760 --> 00:36:20,040
Thank you very much,

276
00:36:20,920 --> 00:36:24,640
but that's alright.
I have my own personal bodyguards.

277
00:36:25,240 --> 00:36:28,120
No matter how good your bodyguards are,

278
00:36:28,720 --> 00:36:31,040
they can only protect you up close.

279
00:36:33,880 --> 00:36:34,960
Thank you so much.

280
00:36:37,120 --> 00:36:38,680
Good cops like you…

281
00:36:40,600 --> 00:36:41,800
are hard to find.

282
00:36:41,880 --> 00:36:44,160
Hardworking people like you

283
00:36:44,680 --> 00:36:46,760
deserve some kind of reward.

284
00:36:50,880 --> 00:36:51,880
There's no need.

285
00:36:52,840 --> 00:36:54,080
It's my duty

286
00:36:55,760 --> 00:36:57,160
to protect the innocent

287
00:36:58,720 --> 00:37:00,120
and catch the guilty.

288
00:37:02,160 --> 00:37:03,480
Good, good.

289
00:37:04,160 --> 00:37:07,240
Our country really needs people like you.

290
00:37:15,360 --> 00:37:18,160
Then, let's head inside.

291
00:37:18,240 --> 00:37:20,040
Oh, yes. After you.

292
00:37:24,040 --> 00:37:25,680
-After you, ma'am.
-Yes.

293
00:37:51,440 --> 00:37:54,960
Take good care
of the police officers out here.

294
00:37:55,040 --> 00:37:57,200
I'm afraid they might not be safe.

295
00:38:31,920 --> 00:38:32,840
Hey.

296
00:38:33,400 --> 00:38:34,600
You can't enter.

297
00:38:37,400 --> 00:38:41,000
Excuse me. Mr. Decha
ordered a birthday cake.

298
00:38:49,280 --> 00:38:50,320
Sir.

299
00:38:50,960 --> 00:38:52,160
What's going on?

300
00:38:53,240 --> 00:38:55,640
Did you order a birthday cake
to surprise Ms. Sirin?

301
00:38:58,200 --> 00:38:59,640
I didn't order it.

302
00:39:53,680 --> 00:39:58,280
If he survives,
I'll have to play my last card.

303
00:40:08,200 --> 00:40:09,400
No!

304
00:40:09,480 --> 00:40:10,960
Scene one, take two.

305
00:40:12,520 --> 00:40:15,520
Hey, let go of me!

306
00:40:31,880 --> 00:40:33,960
-Go low, slam him.
-Slam him down good.

307
00:40:34,040 --> 00:40:36,440
Jump up and kick him down.

308
00:40:36,520 --> 00:40:37,440
Just like that.

309
00:41:04,000 --> 00:41:05,360
I'm sorry.

310
00:41:05,440 --> 00:41:08,440
-That was rough.
-The knife broke?

311
00:41:08,520 --> 00:41:10,480
-Did the knife break?
-You okay?

312
00:41:10,560 --> 00:41:12,200
<i>That was almost perfect.</i>

313
00:41:46,840 --> 00:41:52,280
Subtitle translation by: Anan Pratchayakul
